nd shortfall\\\\n       slows the unlock rather than breaking a schedule; no code reads spend_to_unlock.agent_ratio_n\\\\n       today (#1354).\\\\n     implementations:\\\\n@@ -177,6 +180,7 @@ parameters:\\\\n       eight half-year seasons of 80,000,000 to +48mo; D-0438's four annual tranches of 158,899,000\\\\n       are superseded. Controller and release rules are still undefined\\\\n       (ECON-008 sec. 7 C7, ECON-009 gap G3) and it has no runtime presence yet.\\\\n+      Under D-0531 (closing #1358), the workbook's legacy on-chain referral commission model (6\u201310%) is superseded by a public explorer leaderboard and periodic referral lotteries funded from this reserve and settled off-chain.\\\\n     implementations:\\\\n       - { file: ai-agent-simulator/src/model/parameters.ts, expect: \\\\\\\"FLOP_GENESIS_RESERVE = 800_000_000\\\\\\\" }\\\\n       - { file: ai-agent-simulator/params.yaml, expect: \\\\\\\"reserve_airdrop: 800000000\\\\\\\" }\\\\n@@ -205,11 +209,13 @@ parameters:\\\\n     unit: blocks\\\\n     decision: SPEC-022\\\\n     description: >\\\\n-      90-day linear airdrop vesting duration at 1-second block time. The airdrop-vesting pallet\\\\n-      applies it to every tier today; under yellowpaper \u00a78.2 R8.7 (D-0517, D-0522) no ratified grant\\\\n-      tier uses this duration (Miner and Agent grants unlock against settled sessions with no end\\\\n-      block; Validator grants follow the first-halving freeze and daily release), so it is only the\\\\n-      pallet's interim schedule until R8.7 is implemented.\\\\n+      Interim pallet schedule: 90-day linear airdrop vesting at 1-second block time, governing no\\\\n+      ratified grant tier (\u00a78.2). The airdrop-vesting pallet\\\\n+      applies it to every tier today; under yellowpaper \u00a78.2 R8.7 (D-0517, D-0522, D-0527) no\\\\n+      ratified grant tier uses this duration (Miner grants unlock against miner block rewards and\\\\n+      settled sessions, Agent grants against settled sessions, both with no end block; Validator\\\\n+      grants follow the first-halving freeze and daily release), so it is only the pallet's interim\\\\n+      schedule until R8.7 is implemented.\\\\n     implementations:\\\\n       - { file: pallets/pallets/airdrop-vesting/src/lib.rs, expect: \\\\\\\"VESTING_DURATION_BLOCKS: u32 = 7_776_000\\\\\\\" }\\\\n       - { file: pallets/runtime/zkverify/src/lib.rs,        expect: \\\\\\\"AirdropVestingDurationBlocks: u32 = 7_776_000\\\\\\\" }\\\\n@@ -358,8 +364,7 @@ parameters:\\\\n     rust: STAKER_SHARE_PPT\\\\n     lean: SettlementInt.BlockRewards.stakerPpt\\\\n     description: >\\\\n-      Community-staker share of each block reward (5%; yellowpaper \u00a79) \u2014 all FLOP stakers other\\\\n-      than miners and validators. Decided 2026-08-04, ratified in D-0435 (tokenomics workbook\\\\n+      Community-staker share of each block reward (5%; yellowpaper \u00a79) \u2014 duration-locked community staking pool across seven lock duration tiers with zero slashing risk and no operator delegation (D-0530), for all FLOP stakers other than miners and validators. Decided 2026-08-04, ratified in D-0435 (tokenomics workbook\\\\n       rev 2026-08-20; ECON-008 \u00a72.1, \u00a73 F1) and carved OUT of the miner residual, not added on top. The\\\\n       DISTRIBUTION policy is not ratified: the pallet mints the leg to a sovereign PalletId\\\\n       account and emits an event, pending the F1 design decision. The macro simulator mints the\\\\n@@ -428,13 +433,16 @@ parameters:\\\\n       yellowpaper \u00a79), on top of the 96 FLOP block reward. D-0435 (tokenomics workbook\\\\n       rev 2026-08-20; ECON-008 \u00a72.2) raised it from 5 and made it HALVE with the block reward,\\\\n       on the same 63,072,000-block\\\\n-      halving boundaries; D-0436 then ran it for ALL FIVE halvings instead of three, so it\\\\n+      halving boundaries (`era(b) = \u230ab / H\u230b`); D-0436 then ran it for ALL FIVE halvings instead of three, so it\\\\n       terminates exactly where the reward floors. Per recipient by era: 8 (years 1-2), 4, 2, 1,\\\\n       0.5 (years 9-10), then exactly 0 from era 5. Combined per block: 16, 8, 4, 2, 1, then 0.\\\\n       Era 4's 0.5 FLOP is fractional in FLOP but EXACT in base units (5 \u00d7 10^17 of 10^18), so the\\\\n-      integer shift never truncates. Total over the schedule = 63,072,000 \u00d7 (16+8+4+2+1) =\\\\n-      1,955,232,000 FLOP. Supersedes the 2026-06-24 flat-5, era-0-only decision and D-0435's\\\\n-      three-era cap.\\\\n+      integer shift never truncates. With genesis block 0 unrewarded (R9.7) and exclusive sunset block\\\\n+      `SubsidyEndBlock` = 315,360,000, the subsidy mints on 315,359,999 produced blocks (`1..=315,359,999`,\\\\n+      63,071,999 in era 0 and 63,072,000 in each of eras 1\u20134): total over the schedule =\\\\n+      63,072,000 \u00d7 (16+8+4+2+1) \u2212 16 = 1,955,231,984 FLOP (1,955,232,000 in the H-blocks-per-era closed\\\\n+      form before subtracting unrewarded block 0). Supersedes the 2026-06-24 flat-5, era-0-only decision\\\\n+      and D-0435's three-era cap.\\\\n     implementations:\\\\n       - { file: pallets/pallets/flop-subsidy/src/lib.rs, expect: \\\\\\\"SUBSIDY_INITIAL_PER_BLOCK: u128 = 8_000_000_000_000_000_000\\\\\\\" }\\\\n       - { file: ai-agent-simulator/params.yaml,          expect: \\\\\\\"labs_rate: 8\\\\\\\" }\\\\n@@ -447,11 +455,13 @@ parameters:\\\\n     unit: blocks\\\\n     decision: D-0436\\\\n     description: >\\\\n-      Subsidy minting duration (~3650 days = 10 years = 5 subsidy halving eras), after which it\\\\n-      sunsets automatically. D-0435 extended it from 63,072,000 (~730 days) to 189,216,000 in\\\\n-      lockstep with making the rate halve; D-0436 extended it again to 5 \u00d7 halving_interval_blocks\\\\n-      so the subsidy tracks the reward's halving phase and TERMINATES exactly where the reward\\\\n-      floors (era 5). Unlike the reward it has no floor: era >= 5 pays exactly 0.\\\\n+      Exclusive subsidy sunset block (~3650 days = 10 years = 5 \u00d7 halving_interval_blocks), at and\\\\n+      after which (`now >= SubsidyEndBlock`) `on_initialize` mints 0. With genesis block 0 unrewarded,\\\\n+      produced blocks `1..=315,359,999` (315,359,999 blocks) mint the subsidy. D-0435 extended it from\\\\n+      63,072,000 (~730 days) to 189,216,000 in lockstep with making the rate halve; D-0436 extended it\\\\n+      again to 5 \u00d7 halving_interval_blocks so the subsidy tracks the reward's halving phase and\\\\n+      TERMINATES on the same boundary (`b = 315,360,000`) where the reward floors (era 5). Unlike the\\\\n+      reward it has no floor: era >= 5 pays exactly 0.\\\\n     implementations:\\\\n       - { file: pallets/pallets/flop-subsidy/src/lib.rs, expect: \\\\\\\"SUBSIDY_DURATION_BLOCKS: u64 = 315_360_000\\\\\\\" }\\\\n       - { file: ai-agent-simulator/params.yaml,          expect: \\\\\\\"end_block: 315360000\\\\\\\" }\\\\n@@ -475,7 +485,8 @@ parameters:\\\\n     on_chain: {source_only: Not exported as a FRAME constant; verified against source only.}\\\\n     value: 20\\\\n     unit: percent\\\\n-    description: Maximum commission a miner may charge delegators.\\\\n+    decision: D-0530\\\\n+    description: \\\\\\\"[DEPRECATED \u2014 D-0530] Legacy maximum commission a miner could charge delegators (20%; yellowpaper \u00a76.1). Superseded by the operator self-stake-only ruling (D-0530); retained in pallet-miner-staking source pending legacy delegation removal.\\\\\\\"\\\\n     implementations:\\\\n       - { file: pallets/pallets/miner-staking/src/lib.rs, expect: \\\\\\\"MAX_COMMISSION_RATE: Perbill = Perbill::from_percent(20)\\\\\\\" }\\\\n \\\\n@@ -520,7 +531,7 @@ parameters:\\\\n     on_chain: {constants: [HwCalibration.MinVerifiedJobs]}\\\\n     value: 64\\\\n     unit: jobs\\\\n-    description: \\\\\\\"D-0433 minimum independently verified jobs in the quick serving-entry burst. The separate utilization equation st